lity reasons is a  different question but this is sort of a  mathematical  reality so there would be potential for  aerospace companies who are able to  develop spaceflight technology necessary  to do this and it's undoubtedly one of  their motivations right now  now really no one at this point is  saying that asteroid mining will never  happen we seem to know that it's coming  it's more a matter of when and how we  approach it and how are we going to  figure out who is entitled to lay a  claim to asteroids for ownership right  now NASA estimates our suggests that all  of the asteroids in the solar system  most of which reside in the asteroid  belt between Mars and Jupiter are worth  about 700 quintillion dollars to humans  that's about a hundred billion dollars  of value per person currently on earth  and because most of the solar systems  asteroids are in this belt which is  relatively close to Earth it's realistic  that we'd have the capability of  unlocking at least some of that value  within the current century now there are  some established documents that governs  some of this ownership which we've  already talked about on the show before  you've got the Outer Space Treaty of  1967 that was signed by a hundred and  thirty-two countries no government  nation or state can claim sovereignty of  outer space and celestial bodies like  asteroids the premise around asteroid  limited is that individuals in the  private general public should have the  right to claim the future mining rights  of asteroids today and that it should be  done democratically and that the big  space industry corporations shouldn't be  the only beneficiaries of this just  mind-blowing amount of value resources  and wealth that could come that will  come from mining asteroids asteroid  limited wants us to think about this  being analogous to the internet the  internet itself is owned by no-one but  we can claim dot-com domains you would  have been smart to claim certain domain  in the late 90s and early 2000s because  they would have accumulated a lot of  long-term value but how would someone  stake a claim to an asteroid where would  the records be kept  how are the claims validated these are  the problems that that asteroid limited  wants to solve their answer is  blockchain asteroid limited sees itself  as modeling this process after I can ICA  and and that's the organization that  maintains the databases to facilitate  allocating internet namespaces like  domains the asteroid limited blockchain  would be immutable it's a decentralized  ledger that would store the claims there  are 600,000 asteroids in the solar  system that have already been identified  and catalogued and you could codify them  in this blockchain ledger the asteroid  limited smart contract would enable a  cryptocurrency called aster coins which  could be used to buy and sell these  claims and here are the specifics of how  it would work a person would obtain  what's called a block claim from  asteroid limited which will keep within  the asteroid limited blockchain  ecosystem the record of your claim to  the future mining rights of the asteroid  the block claim is a proprietary  mechanism to the Aster coin ecosystem  and the idea is that the ecosystems  cryptocurrency the Aster coin would be  one of the first self-sustaining kryptos  in contrast to something like Bitcoin  which merely functions as virtual gold  or an asset that can be held and  converted back into fiat as needed  asteroid limited believes that the block  claim economy would operate more like a  fiat currency where value is judged  based on the buying power of the  currency the cost of one block claim  registration will be fixed to one aster  coin regardless of the value of the  Aster coin when it was obtained in the  market once the Aster coin is collected  as payment it would then cycle back into  the market through asteroid limited  Treasury so every block  block lane registration is secured by an  aster coin on asteroid limited aetherium  blockchain which is what would promote  the regular usage and liquidity and  growth of aster coin as a currency at  least that's the goal the idea would be  that as space exploration grows so would  the value of a stroke Oien we would have  immediate liquidity through consistent  registrations of blocked claims but the  real potential would be in the  possibility of aster coin continuing to  be circulated long term right now the  more than 600,000 identified asteroids  in the solar system are valued by what's  called spectral analysis which takes  into account the composition of the  asteroid it's mining attributes its  trajectory and distance from the earth  at different future points in time upon  the launch of the block claim ledger  each asteroids value would be  apportioned into a certain number of  block claim tokens each token token  representing 1 million u.s. dollars of  value with each individual block claim  at a price of one aster coin per claim  so for example I think this is best  illuminated via an example if you have  an asteroid that has 82 billion dollars  of estimated value these are actually  not unrealistic numbers for the value of  an asteroids contents and a block claim  is valued at 1 million dollars that  asteroid would have a total of 82,000  block claim tokens available for  registration each of those block claim  tokens is a fractional mathematical  representation of an asteroid expressed  as a percentage of the total claim over  time as the asteroid Ledger evolves  valuation modeling of the claim would  increase based on the number of claims  that are left on that asteroid its  proximity to earth the market value of  its composition which of course would be  affected by the prices of precious  metals here on earth and this would  create a sort of natural demand for  certain asteroids which are more viable  to mine on the basis of their  characteristics so once a block claim is  registered a claim will be identified  and stored in an immune  record cryptographically secured in the  blockchain via that block claim token  and the value of the block camp claim  could be tracked via asteroid Limited's  online platform and their registration  data set the asteroid block claim  exchange would allow individual block  claims to be traded and exchanged in an  online marketplace through potential  mining coops that are established by  claimants as well the goal would be to  position the Aster token as a  transactional currency currency both  presently through the block claim  mechanism as well as in the future were  it to become the digital currency of  mining asteroids the block claim  mechanism would closely parallel the  registry that I can use is to register  internet don't domains on the block  claim platform asteroid limited will  provide a lookup table which they call a  who claim for the public recording of  claims and the provision of private  prohibitions when desired by the  claimant for a small fee the lookup  table would include data like the  asteroids name the type its distance  from Earth its my noble value the  diameter its composition the registered  block claim value the date the block  claim was created the expiration date  for the registrar the names of any  resellers right now the idea is that  each aster token has an intrinsic value  of about a thousand US dollars due to  the 200 billion dollars worth of block  claims that would be held in reserve by  asteroid limited through their  registration of 200 thousand block  claims following the launch of the  platform as asteroid limited sees it  aster coin would then have a life beyond  the IC o---- unlike many tokens being  created through AI cos these days  because aster coins will be the only  supported cryptocurrency for making  block claims as we speak about what  asteroid limited is working on they are  working on the completion of the  asteroid block claim ecosystem  development in order to launch that  claim 